 "⚠️_THIS_IS_A_REHEARSAL_NOT_A_RESULT": "Ten sentences I wrote myself, with off-menu labels I also wrote — the coverage number on this set measures my own answer key. n=10 gives the disagreement rate a RESOLUTION of 0.1: one utterance flipping moves it a whole tenth. The Bedrock arm read 0.2 and then 0.1 on two runs of the same ten sentences twenty minutes apart, which is the resolution talking, not the model. Separating 0.10 from 0.20 at 80%% power needs n=199 utterances per arm; 0.10 from 0.15 needs 686. Nothing here is quotable as a classifier comparison.",
 "why_three_arms": "opus-4-7 on Bedrock REJECTS temperature, so the paid arm cannot be pinned. The local arm is therefore run at BOTH 0.0 and 1.0: at 0.0 its replicate disagreement is 0 BY CONSTRUCTION, and comparing that to an unpinnable arm would be a comparison of samplers."
